        }
      ],
      "message": "util: cap Sock::WaitMany timeout\n\nbitcoin-cli turns -rpcclienttimeout=0 into a 5 year timeout and passes\nit down to Sock::Wait. On systems without poll() (e.g. macOS and the\nBSDs) the wait is done with select(), which fails with EINVAL for\ntimeouts above 10^8 seconds on macOS. So since the libevent removal in\n#34342, `bitcoin-cli -rpcclienttimeout=0 ...` fails on macOS with\n\"Could not connect to the server\". With poll(), the millisecond count\nis narrowed to int, so large values can wrap as well.\n\nCap the timeout at INT_MAX milliseconds (about 24.8 days), which fits\npoll() and stays below the 31 days that POSIX requires select() to\naccept.",
